          "title": "Special attacks and qualities mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Scent · The rat detects nearby enemies by smell. The adventure refers to the Dungeon Master’s Guide for the general scent rules."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Barrels 2 and 5 · Four rats hide in each barrel. They stay inside until disturbed, then attack. Each of the eight rats has 1 HP.",
            "Contagious in this adventure · A creature that comes into contact with this animal must make a DC 13 Fortitude save against the Burning Plague. See the adventure’s disease rules on pp. 3–4."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "Neutral. Weapon Finesse (bite).",
            "The adventure prints CR 1 on the collective Rats (8) line. It gives no CR for a single rat.",
            "The rat’s printed bite is 1d3 - 4. Its Hide modifier is +18.",
            "Miguel Duran, The Burning Plague (Wizards of the Coast, 2000), Area 4: The Larder, pp. 7–8."
          ]
        }
